{"w":2400,"h":3406,"lines":[{"x":0.051546391973246994,"w":0.016494844754536941,"h":0.013081395479068947,"y":0.40552325561802371,"c":1,"t":"F"},{"c":1,"h":0.015916792981007122,"x":0.86766937770453112,"t":"Reading","y":0.040256840736717869,"w":0.091358776092529292},{"c":1,"h":0.017441861012089777,"x":0.10103093953366331,"w":0.80412368774414056,"t":"Archaeologists Terry Hunt of the University of Hawaii and Carl Lipo of California","y":0.088662790421798365},{"x":0.10721649154417055,"w":0.78556701660156247,"t":"State University agree that Easter Island lost its lush forests and that it was an","y":0.1074574283381412,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1},{"y":0.12354651194534572,"h":0.020348836167448092,"c":1,"x":0.10309277712189925,"t":"'ecological catastrophe' - but they believe the islanders themselves weren't to","w":0.78556701660156258},{"t":"blame. And the moai certainly weren't. Archaeological excavations indicate that the","w":0.83092783610026033,"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"x":0.10721649421554408,"y":0.14533176755829502},{"t":"Rapanui went to heroic efforts to protect the resources of their wind-lashed, infertile","h":0.020315435726503961,"x":0.10715758907333585,"y":0.16154964472541766,"w":0.83722371419270836,"c":1},{"t":"fields. They built thousands of circular stone windbreaks and gardened inside them,","h":0.019240051735448516,"y":0.1804713646928876,"x":0.10304075555024146,"w":0.84343643188476569,"c":1},{"w":0.78350514729817722,"h":0.017615971814445186,"y":0.20052847930448225,"t":"and used broken volcanic rocks to keep the soil moist. In short, Hunt and Lipo","c":1,"x":0.1051546429002488},{"c":1,"h":0.019014751638164906,"y":0.21805203774411908,"w":0.69082946777343746,"x":0.10508757621739648,"t":"argue, the prehistoric Rapanui were pioneers of sustainable farming."},{"t":"Hunt and Lipo contend that moal-building was an activity that helped keep the","x":0.10309278025426143,"w":0.78556701660156258,"y":0.24854651179506504,"h":0.015988371754420583,"c":1},{"w":0.79381444295247394,"h":0.017441861012089777,"t":"peace between islanders. They also believe that moving the moai required few","c":1,"x":0.10309277842678853,"y":0.26598837181694868},{"t":"people and no wood, because they were walked upright. On that issue, Hunt and","h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1,"y":0.28479154408373808,"x":0.10309277973795399,"w":0.81649485270182298},{"h":0.020497318162542855,"x":0.10303544462312639,"w":0.82691991170247381,"y":0.30092787532184895,"c":1,"t":"Lipo say, archaeological evidence backs up Rapanui folklore. Recent experiments"},{"c":1,"t":"indicate that as few as 18 people could, with three strong ropes and a bit of","w":0.76288660685221354,"y":0.32119788609238653,"h":0.017464904874755716,"x":0.10103092334666144},{"y":0.33998825627642248,"t":"practice, easily manoeuvre a 1,000 kg moai replica a few hundred metres. The","x":0.10309277843707131,"w":0.79381444295247394,"h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"figures' fat bellies tilted them forward, and a D-shaped base allowed handlers to roll","x":0.10302849633697661,"y":0.35741280237977036,"h":0.019948095835732205,"w":0.84135162353515636},{"y":0.3764995349896425,"c":1,"x":0.10296287661136053,"t":"and rock them side to side.","w":0.27657966613769536,"h":0.017464388557832944},{"x":0.10309278119356359,"y":0.40546095142658833,"w":0.72371134440104168,"t":"Moreover, Hunt and Lipo are convinced that the settlers were not wholly","h":0.017615971814445075,"c":1},{"w":0.82061854044596372,"h":0.017448688491400133,"c":1,"y":0.42441860437492496,"t":"responsible for the loss of the island's trees. Archaeological finds of nuts from the","x":0.10103093586111858},{"w":0.7918686930338541,"x":0.10097790133771592,"y":0.44156981492545477,"h":0.020226811774674336,"t":"extinct Easter Island palm show tiny grooves, made by the teeth of Polynesian","c":1},{"y":0.46065766317372114,"w":0.83298970540364592,"h":0.019083969465648831,"c":1,"x":0.10103092063764686,"t":"rats. The rats arrived along with the settlers, and in just a few years, Hunt and Lipo"},{"c":1,"t":"calculate, they would have overrun the island. They would have prevented the","x":0.1010309177291694,"w":0.78762888590494784,"h":0.017441861012089888,"y":0.47965116251070272},{"x":0.10103094390072935,"t":"reseeding of the slow-growing palm trees and thereby doomed Rapa Nui's forest,","w":0.82061854044596361,"y":0.49706400495628134,"h":0.018924367056828206,"c":1},{"w":0.80618555704752604,"c":1,"t":"even without the settlers' campaign of deforestation. No doubt the rats ate birds'","x":0.1030927884270405,"y":0.51453488356117871,"h":0.018935462830700911},{"w":0.81248270670572909,"h":0.019164756824182061,"x":0.10098172517165163,"y":0.53336399223976361,"c":1,"t":"eggs too. Hunt and Lipo also see no evidence that Rapanui civilisation collapsed"},{"t":"when the palm forest did. They think its population grew rapidly and then remained","x":0.10097798911900052,"w":0.83309453328450522,"y":0.55222927691638601,"h":0.018828259309599527,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"more or less stable until the arrival of the Europeans, who introduced deadly","w":0.76931060791015615,"y":0.56931061730979027,"h":0.021884194697202486,"x":0.1009218896466292},{"h":0.020018588215620192,"y":0.58886655087148965,"c":1,"x":0.10095140364722748,"w":0.8290344746907552,"t":"diseases to which islanders had no immunity. Then in the nineteenth century slave"},{"c":1,"x":0.10103091516417294,"y":0.60892542566432883,"t":"traders decimated the population, which shrivelled to 111 people by 1877.","w":0.74226806640624998,"h":0.017615971814445075},{"c":1,"w":0.79612965901692712,"x":0.10089553386256379,"y":0.63451933807025707,"t":"Hunt and Lipo's vision, therefore, is one of an island populated by peacetul and","h":0.022143416032326391},{"w":0.81649485270182287,"h":0.017441861012089777,"c":1,"x":0.096907212672607934,"y":0.65552325553669155,"t":"ingenious moai builders and careful stewards of the land, rather than by reckless"},{"x":0.10103093218390569,"w":0.83711339314778654,"h":0.017462344570014277,"t":"destroyers ruining their own environment and society. 'Rather than a case of abject","y":0.67439812081748629,"c":1},{"x":0.098909010821726984,"w":0.84342427571614587,"c":1,"y":0.6904845171565388,"t":"failure, Rapu Nui is an unlikely story of success', they claim. Whichever is the case,","h":0.020290665954123877},{"w":0.8329897054036457,"c":1,"t":"there are surely some valuable lessons which the world at large can learn from the","x":0.098969064719039754,"h":0.015988371754420583,"y":0.71220930249286918},{"w":0.18598322550455731,"t":"story of Rapa Nui.","h":0.019174068448687742,"x":0.098707007454727602,"c":1,"y":0.72841683104950361},{"h":0.023628416302199917,"c":1,"w":0.29167673746744793,"x":0.3520980615377719,"y":0.9533535445516701,"t":"leltsresources.org"},{"x":0.91340206226611997,"t":"47","c":1,"h":0.013081395479068947,"y":0.94622093005843066,"w":0.026804122924804719}]}